WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.630
Fire an alpha particle
straight at a gold nucleus.

2
00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:05.040
Both are positive.

3
00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:07.880
The alpha particle
carries 2 units of charge,

4
00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:10.150
the nucleus 79.

5
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:13.300
As it closes in, the repulsion slows it.

6
00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:16.900
Its kinetic energy turns into
electric potential energy.

7
00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.110
For an instant, it stops.

8
00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.820
Then it is pushed back the way it came.

9
00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:24.430
How close does it get before it stops?

10
00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.880
Could it ever touch the nucleus?

11
00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:30.030
In this mission, you'll
measure work in electronvolts,

12
00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:33.320
and add up the energy of
a whole group of charges.

13
00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:38.610
Then you'll read equipotential maps, and
use energy to find the closest approach.

14
00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:43.230
Your mission: calculate how close the
alpha particle gets to the nucleus.
